---
layout: base.njk
title: Who said it
description: Every claim on Miżien is matched to the body or person who made it. Government, agencies, regulators, parties, NGOs, business and media, with their claims and the bodies their claims connect to.
permalink: /bodies/
styles: [who.css]
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as m -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Who said it</li></ol>
</nav>

<article class="page prose-page bodies-index">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Who said it</p>
    <h1>Bodies and people</h1>
    <p class="lead">Every claim is matched to the body or person who made it: {{ mizien.bodies | where("kind", "organisation") | length }}
      bodies and {{ mizien.bodies | where("kind", "person") | length }} people so far, from government and its agencies to
      parties, NGOs, business and the media. Every side is held to the same standard.</p>
  </header>

  <aside class="notice" aria-label="What these pages show">
    <p><strong>A record, not a score.</strong> Claims are picked because they are public and can be checked, not to
      sample anyone's statements fairly. A body with more claims here has simply been checked more often; the bars
      summarise the checks so far, not anyone's accuracy in general. <a href="/methodology/connections/#bodies">How
      claims are matched to bodies</a>.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="who-key" aria-labelledby="h-key">
    <h2 id="h-key" class="visually-hidden">How to read the cards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Verdict bar</b> from {{ 5 }} checked claims: how many checks ended in each verdict, as counts.</li>
      <li><b>Tentative balance</b> at 3 or 4: where the checks so far sit between Contradicted and Supported, recent
        claims counting more (by the date of the claim, not of the check). Work in progress, not a rating.
        <a href="/methodology/connections/#summaries">How it is worked out</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Pledges</b> keep their own labels (on track, off track, not measurable…), always shown, never mixed into the
        verdicts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  {%- set ps = mizien.pledges | pledgeStack(mizien.claims) %}
  {%- if ps %}
  <section class="pstack-sec" aria-labelledby="h-pledges">
    <h2 id="h-pledges">Pledges, year by year</h2>
    <p>Each disk is a year in which pledges were made, the newest on top; each dot is a pledge, coloured by its label,
      with a ring in the colour of the verdict on the facts it rests on, where those were checked. Pledges on the same
      topic sit at the same place on every disk, so similar pledges line up; lines join them across the years,
      coloured by the average verdict of their facts (dashed: none checked yet).</p>
    {%- include "pledge-stack.njk" %}
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <p class="see-also">{% icon "pattern" %}<a href="/bodies/patterns/">Patterns by kind of body</a>: which pattern
    tags, verdicts and topics turn up in claims by each kind of body, and what each side said, when, on each issue.</p>

  <p class="small">On the <a href="/explore/?group=speaker">claims web</a>, group the claims by <em>Who said it</em> to see the same
    register as a constellation: each kind of body is a hub, each body orbits it, and people sit beside the body they spoke for.</p>

  {%- for t in mizien.body_types %}
  {%- set orgs = mizien.bodies | where("type", t.id) | where("kind", "organisation") %}
  {%- set people = mizien.bodies | where("type", t.id) | where("kind", "person") %}
  {%- if orgs.length or people.length %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-{{ t.id }}">
    <h2 id="h-{{ t.id }}">{{ t.label }}</h2>
    <ul class="body-grid">
      {%- for o in orgs %}
      {%- set s = o | whoSummary(mizien.pledges, mizien.bodies) %}
      <li class="body-card who-card">
        <a class="bc-name" href="{{ o.path }}">{{ o.name }}</a>
        {%- if o.parent %}<span class="bc-parent">part of {{ o.parent.name }}</span>{% endif %}
        <span class="bc-count">{{ s.total }} claim{% if s.total != 1 %}s{% endif %} · {{ s.checked }} checked</span>
        {%- set big = false %}{% include "who-meter.njk" %}
        {%- if o.people.length %}
        <span class="bc-people">{% for x in o.people %}<a href="{{ x.path }}">{{ x.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</article>
